### `333 service install`: whether the program a service would run is still there tomorrow.
##
## A line here ends in `{` and the next begins with `""}` where the printed line is
## wider than a line of this file may be; the placeable spanning the two prints no
## line break.

service-exe-asking = asking the system where this program is

service-exe-fleeting = this program is running from { $exe }, which is { $why }. {
    ""}A service pointed at it would stop the day that goes. Copy it to { $home } {
    ""}and run `service install` from there.

service-exe-emptied = a directory the system empties
service-exe-build-directory = a build directory, which the next build or clean replaces
